    "statementHTML": "<div class=\"statement-body\">\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-goal\">\n   <h2><span class=\"icon icon-goal\">&nbsp;</span><span>Goal </span></h2>\n   <span class=\"question-statement\">In a tree, <const>@</const> forms the crown and <const>#</const> forms the trunk. Ignore all other characters.<br><br><strong>Guaranteed:</strong> tree rows are consecutive, centered, solid blocks of <const>@</const> or <const>#</const>. Crown rows have odd widths and precede any trunk rows.<br><br>A valid tree has crown rows of widths <const>1</const>, <const>3</const>, <const>5</const>, ... and trunk rows of width <const>1</const>, with at least one row of each. The crown may stop early.<br><br>If valid, print all tree row widths from top to bottom, separated by spaces. Otherwise, print <const>INVALID</const>.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-protocol\">\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-input\"><strong>Line 1:</strong> Two integers <var>h</var> and <var>w</var>, the picture's height and odd width.<br><strong>Next <var>h</var> lines:</strong> A string <var>row</var> of exactly <var>w</var> characters.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-output\"><strong>One line:</strong> The crown and trunk row widths, separated by spaces, or <const>INVALID</const>.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Constraints</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-constraints\">1 &le; <var>h</var>, <var>w</var> &le; 31<br><var>w</var> is odd.<br>Each <var>row</var> contains exactly <var>w</var> printable ASCII characters, possibly including spaces.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Example</div>\n      <div class=\"statement-inout\">\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-in\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n       